course: dictionary
lesson: 6298
title: Words that do not change in the plural
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Most nouns add an -s to show more than one: one cat, two cats. Some nouns do not change at all. «One moose, two moose» is correct, so moose stays the same for one animal or for many.
explain: You can tell how many there are from the number, or from the small words "is" and "are". «The moose is huge» means one moose, and «the moose are huge» means more than one.
explain: Moose live in forests and wetlands of Canada, Alaska, the northern USA, and northern Europe and Asia. In Britain the same animal is called elk. A moose is a very large deer, and it can stand over 2 metres at the shoulder.
fact: Moose is a noun, and its plural is also moose.
fact: Other nouns that do not change in the plural include sheep and deer.
fact: «The moose, called elk in Britain, is the largest deer.»
fact: Moose eat leaves, twigs and water plants, and they are good swimmers.
fact: Moose can be dangerous, so keep far away from them.
exercise: Pick the correct plural: two ___ crossed the road. | moosies | meese | mooses | *moose
exercise: «The moose ___ huge.» Which word fits one moose? | be | *is | are | were
exercise: What is a moose? | A lake in Canada | A kind of tree | *A very large deer with long legs | A small grey bird
test: «Crashes with moose are dangerous because long legs put the heavy body at windscreen height.» Why are these crashes dangerous? | *The heavy body is at windscreen height | Moose cannot run | Moose are small and hard to see | Roads are too narrow for cars
test: Which word does not change in the plural? | dogs | *deer | cats | boxes
exam: Ella reads: «The moose, called elk in Britain, is the largest deer.» What does elk mean in Britain? | A kind of fish | A small bird | *Another name for moose | A type of tree
